 "text": "Hello, how are you doing? Totally normal. Social events make fear worse because there are people around to notice. Small ones that everyone does. You check someone's name before sitting down, your phone in the kitchen, and you ask for water before you get it. Ask to explain, and say you'd love forte if it looks too grand. Lots of people do, and it makes you feel so much cooler. Order something you like simple, and say in front of the waiter so you remember the name. Then ask for it well done if that's how you like it.",
